==Portuguese==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|pt|accordar||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|acordar}}, from {{inh|pt|VL.|*accordāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|*accordō}}, from {{inh|pt|la|cor}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/ɐ.kuɾ.ˈdaɾ/|[ɐ.kuɾ.ˈðaɾ]|lang=pt}}
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|/ˌa.koʁ.ˈda(ʁ)/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|a|cor|dar|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|acord|ar}}

# {{senseid|pt|to gain consciousness}} {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to {{l|en|awake}}; to {{l|en|wake up}} {{gloss|to stop sleeping}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''Acordei''' às sete da manhã.|inline=1|'''I woke up''' at seven in the morning.}}
#: {{syn|pt|despertar}} {{q|more formal}}
#: {{ant|pt|adormecer|cair no sono|dormir}}
# {{senseid|pt|to cause to wake up}} {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|wake}}; to {{l|en|wake up}}; to {{l|en|awaken}} {{gloss|to cause someone to stop sleeping}}
#* {{RQ:mul:Rowling Harry Potter|pt-BR|3|page=336|text=Francamente, vão '''acordar''' todo mundo!|t=Honestly, you're going '''to wake''' everyone '''up'''!}}
#: {{ux|pt|Não faça barulho, senão pode '''acordar''' os vizinhos.|inline=1|Don’t make noise, or you could '''wake''' the neighbours '''up'''.}}
#: {{syn|pt|despertar}} {{q|more formal}}
#: {{ant|pt|ninar}}
# {{senseid|pt|to become aware of a serious issue}} {{indtr|pt|para|intr=1}} to {{l|en|wake up}} (to) {{gloss|to become aware of a serious issue}}
#: {{ux|pt|O país inteiro '''acorda''' para o terrorismo.|inline=1|The whole country is '''waking up''' to [the problem of] terrorism.}}
#: {{syn|pt|despertar}}
# {{senseid|pt|to stop being sleepy}} {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to {{l|en|wake up}} {{gloss|to stop being sleepy}}
#: {{ux|pt|Tomei um café para '''acordar'''.|inline=1|I drank some coffee to '''wake myself up'''.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to cause to stop being sleepy}} {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|wake up}} {{gloss|to cause to stop being sleepy}}
#: {{ux|pt|Só um energético consegue me '''acordar'''.|inline=1|Only an energy drink can '''wake''' me '''up'''.}}
# {{senseid|pt|to arouse}} {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|instigate}}; to {{l|en|stir up}} {{gloss|to incite feelings}}
#: {{ux|pt|Os eventos '''acordaram''' a raiva dos franceses.|inline=1|The events '''stirred up''' the anger of the French.}}
#: {{syn|pt|instigar}}
# {{senseid|pt|to accord}} {{lb|pt|transitive}} to {{l|en|accord}} {{gloss|to bring into accord}}
#: {{ux|pt|Os inimigos tiveram que '''acordar''' suas diferenças.|inline=1|The enemies had to '''accord''' their differences.}}
#: {{syn|pt|concordar|harmonizar}}
# {{pt-verb-form-of|acordar}}

